abstract = {In 1985 Mark Spinrad and Curt Abraham published; "The Wild West Lifecycle (WILI)" [1] which, although written with a slightly irreverent tongue-in-cheek style, introduced a significant metaphor for the software engineering lifecycle. In this paper we will discuss briefly the importance of software metaphors in general, and then revisit and expand the Wild West analogy.},
