	doi = {https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-012225261-7/50009-9},
	abstract = {Publisher Summary This chapter deals with electroabsorption (EA) modulators. It presents a wide variety of research on current and future applications for electroabsorption modulators. EA modulators offer advantages over other modulator types in size, cost, drive voltage, and compatibility with monolithic integration. The chapter examines a conceptual system to understand the role of EA modulated sources in fiber optic communication systems. It reveals that a generic optical communication system is composed of three main parts: a transmitter, a communication channel, and a receiver. A simple conceptual diagram of a fiber optic communication system is illustrated. The chapter distinguishes between principle of EA modulators and electrooptic modulators. One of the greatest benefits of EA modulators is the ease with which they can be integrated with other components. Complex integrated devices that combine EA modulators with lasers, semiconductor optical amplifiers, and other EA modulators to perform more complex data modulation functions are also described.},
