	abstract = {Publisher Summary This chapter provides extensive coverage of existing mobile wireless technologies. It illustrates that mobile wireless is probably the most active area in the domain of computing and communications. The chapter emphasizes on the highly anticipated 3G cellular networks and widely deployed wireless local area networks (LANs), as the next-generation smart phones are likely to offer at least these two types of connectivity. It also highlights the technical details of the state of the art of many wireless technologies, including cellular, wireless LANs,wireless MANs, Bluetooth, UWB, satellite, wireless sensor networks, and RFID. Moreover, this chapter explains how the technology works, how it compares to other competing or complementary technologies. It also investigates the possible applications are that can take advantage of the technology. This chapter concludes by presenting a list of standards in the wireless arena.},
