	issn = {0045-7949},
	url = {https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/004579499290386E},
	doi = {https://doi.org/10.1016/0045-7949(92)90386-E},
	abstract = {This paper presents a new technique for reducing the bandwidth and profile of a symmetric and sparse matrix. A graph representation of the matrix is decomposed into a group of isolated sets by general level structures. These are exploited to construct a maximal-depth partitioned structure, each level of which has as equal width as possible. Then, the vertices of the partitioned structure are numbered consecutively. The presented method is more complicated than the well-known GPS algorithm, but it can provide a more reliable procedure to reduce the bandwidth. The bandwidth reduced by the presented method is smaller than or equal to the one reduced by the GPS. Examples are included to illustrate in detail the presented algorithms.},
