	doi = {https://doi.org/10.1016/S1388-3437(97)80012-1},
	abstract = {We propose an algorithm for connection admission control (CAC) in the case where connections are of the variable bit rate (VBR) type and the trunk carrying the multiplexed VBR connections is itself a VBR connection. The latter assumption occurs for example when a number of ATM connections is multiplexed over one VBR virtual path connection, or when a number of IP/RSVP flows is multiplexed over one VBR virtual channel connection. The algorithm is based on the proportional allocation method. We apply the algorithm to compare on some examples the multiplexing gain obtained by (1) aggregating a number of VBR connections into a VBR trunk (2) into a CBR trunk or (3) without aggregation. These preliminary results show that the use of VBR trunks makes it possible to aggregate a number of connections into one without sacrificing bandwidth efficiency.},
